ed measurements of the same animals.\",\"The report itself demonstrates the issue: it states '6 trials per animal', tabulates six rows per animal_id, and the Notes say 'Each trial contributes one observation to the test above', so the pooling of within-animal repeats into the row-independent test is shown in the selected report.\",\"Per-animal right-arm shares range 0.333 to 1.000, showing between-animal heterogeneity that makes the independence violation consequential rather than incidental.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column animal_id exists in the frozen data with six distinct animals (AMB-01..AMB-06), each contributing six rows, matching the stated design; the declaration correctly identifies the level at which rows cluster.","The selected result is an exact binomial test pooling all 36 trials as independent Bernoulli observations, a row-independent procedure applied to rows that are repeated measurements of the same animals.","The report itself demonstrates the issue: it states '6 trials per animal', tabulates six rows per animal_id, and the Notes say 'Each trial contributes one observation to the test above', so the pooling of within-animal repeats into the row-independent test is shown in the selected report.","Per-animal right-arm shares range 0.333 to 1.000, showing between-animal heterogeneity that makes the independence violation consequential rather than incidental.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":4869,"ttft_stream_ms":1667,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":17027,"uuid":"331d9f95-091b-4875-9e51-c61f2aaf9339"}
